.TH LOCATED 1 "2025-02-06" "0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
located \- device location tracking server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B located
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B located
is a lightweight HTTP server for registering and locating mobile devices.
It stores device registrations in a SQLite database and exposes a JSON API.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR daemon ", " \-d
Start the HTTP server in the foreground.
Blocks until SIGINT or SIGTERM is received.
.TP
.B devices
List all registered devices.
Requires a running daemon; uses curl to query the API.
.TP
.BI locate " id"
Request location of the device with the given
.IR id .
Requires a running daemon.
.TP
.BR help ", " \-h
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR version ", " \-v
Print version and exit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " path"
Path to the JSON configuration file.
May appear anywhere in the argument list.
Default: uses built-in defaults (port 8080, db ./devices.db).
.SH CONFIGURATION
The config file is JSON with the following keys:
.TP
.B listen_port
TCP port for the HTTP server (default: 8080).
.TP
.B db_path
Path to the SQLite database file (default: ./devices.db).
.TP
.B api_key
API key for authentication (not enforced in Phase 1).
.SH API ENDPOINTS
.TP
.B POST /api/register
Register a new device. JSON body must include
.BR id ", " token ", and " platform
(android or ios).
Optional:
.BR name .
Returns the device record including a generated
.BR secret .
.TP
.B DELETE /api/register/<id>
Unregister a device by its id.
.TP
.B GET /api/devices
List all registered devices as a JSON array.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/located.json
Default configuration file location (if no \-c given, built-in defaults are used).
.TP
.I ./devices.db
Default SQLite database location.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (invalid arguments, config parse failure, database error, etc.).
.SH AUTHORS
Written for the allardtrac project.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR sqlite3 (1)
